  "id": "backward-pairing",
  "term": "backward pairing",
  "definition": "Backward pairing is a conditioning arrangement in which the unconditioned stimulus is presented before the conditioned stimulus, such as sucrose followed by an odor. In the supplied source, this order is linked to inhibitory learning, meaning the later cue can come to reduce or interrupt the conditioned response rather than trigger it.",
